      "problem": "Solve for $x$ where $\\sqrt{x-4}=2.$",
      "worked_solution": "Squaring both sides of the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x-4} & =2 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{x-4})}^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ x-4 & =4 \\\\ x & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check the result by plugging it into the original equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{8-4} & \\overset{?}{=}2 \\\\ \\sqrt{4} & \\overset{?}{=}2 \\\\ 2 & =2\\,\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe value $x=8$ satisfies the original equation, so we can accept it as a solution.\n\nTherefore, the solution to $\\sqrt{x-4}=2$  is $x=8.$",
